@meta
id: 17-06
title: The jumplist crosses files
chapter: 17
type: lesson
skills: jumplist
par: 100
minutes: 7
vscode: Go to Definition into another file, edit, Alt+Left
open: order.provider.ts payment.service.ts
vimrc: set hidden

@brief
`PaymentService.refund` is going to need the amount as well as the
order id. `refundPartial` in the provider already passes one; `cancel`
does not.

Search for `refund(` in the provider and you are on the call in
`cancel`. That is the line you will finish on. First, switch to the
payment service, find its `refund(` signature, and add
`amount: number` to it. On the line below, the request body
`{ orderId }` becomes `{ orderId, amount }`.

Then come back to the provider, to the exact line you left, and pass
`order.total` as the second argument. Do not search for it again, and
do not switch buffers by name. The jumplist knows which file you came
from.

Both files are open as buffers. Both are graded.

@keys
| `:b payment` | switch to the buffer whose name contains `payment` |
| `Ctrl-O` | back one jump, even if that jump was into another file |
| `t}` | up to just before the closing brace |
| `:wqa` | write everything and quit |

@hints
Switching buffers is a jump. So is the search you do inside the service
to find the signature. Count them.
--
Two `Ctrl-O`. The first undoes the search inside the service and puts
you at the top of it; the second crosses back into the provider. Watch
the file name in the status line change.
--
`/refund(` Enter, `:b payment` Enter, `/refund(` Enter,
`f)i, amount: number` Esc, `j` `t}i, amount` Esc, `Ctrl-O` `Ctrl-O`,
`f)i, order.total` Esc, `:wqa`.

@solution
    /refund(<Enter> :b payment<Enter> /refund(<Enter>
    f)i, amount: number<Esc> jt}i, amount<Esc>
    Ctrl-O Ctrl-O f)i, order.total<Esc> :wqa<Enter>

The jumplist belongs to the window, not to the file, so it records
positions in every buffer you have visited from it. `:jumps` shows a
file name against each entry. `Ctrl-O` steps through them without
caring which file they are in, and when the next entry is in a
different buffer it switches for you.

This is the Go to Definition workflow from VS Code, done with a search
and a buffer switch instead of a language server. Chapter 18 gives you
better ways to open the other file; the way *back* will still be
`Ctrl-O`, and it will still be exact to the character.

Why two presses. The search you did inside the service was a jump from
line 1 of that file, so the list holds three positions: the provider
line, the top of the service, and the signature. Going back one lands
on the top of the service; going back two lands home. If that feels
like counting, the next lesson gives you a way that does not need it.

This lesson set `hidden` for you so that leaving the service with
unsaved changes is allowed. Without it vim refuses to switch away from
a modified buffer, and `Ctrl-O` silently stays put. Most people set it
in their vimrc on day one; chapter 28 covers why.

@start order.provider.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { OrderRepository } from './order.repository';
import { CustomerProvider } from '../customer/customer.provider';
import { PaymentService } from '../../infrastructure/services/payment.service';
import { EmailService } from '../../infrastructure/services/email.service';

@injectable()
export class OrderProvider {
  constructor(
    @inject(OrderRepository) protected orderRepository: OrderRepository,
    @inject(CustomerProvider) protected customerProvider: CustomerProvider,
    @inject(PaymentService) protected paymentService: PaymentService,
    @inject(EmailService) protected emailService: EmailService,
  ) {}

  public async findOne(id: string) {
    const order = await this.orderRepository.findOne({ where: { id } });

    if (!order) {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_FOUND');
    }

    return order;
  }

  public async create(args: { customerId: string; total: number }) {
    const customer = await this.customerProvider.findOne(args.customerId);

    const order = await this.orderRepository.create({
      values: { customerId: customer.id, total: args.total, status: 'PENDING' },
    });

    await this.emailService.send({ orderId: order.id, template: 'order_confirmation' });

    return order;
  }

  public async cancel(id: string) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);

    if (order.status === 'SHIPPED') {
      throw exception('ORDER_ALREADY_SHIPPED');
    }

    await this.paymentService.refund(order.id);

    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id },
      values: { status: 'CANCELLED' },
    });
  }

  public async refundPartial(id: string, amount: number) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);

    if (amount > order.total) {
      throw exception('REFUND_EXCEEDS_TOTAL');
    }

    await this.paymentService.refund(order.id, amount);

    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id },
      values: { refundedAmount: amount },
    });
  }
}

@expected order.provider.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { OrderRepository } from './order.repository';
import { CustomerProvider } from '../customer/customer.provider';
import { PaymentService } from '../../infrastructure/services/payment.service';
import { EmailService } from '../../infrastructure/services/email.service';

@injectable()
export class OrderProvider {
  constructor(
    @inject(OrderRepository) protected orderRepository: OrderRepository,
    @inject(CustomerProvider) protected customerProvider: CustomerProvider,
    @inject(PaymentService) protected paymentService: PaymentService,
    @inject(EmailService) protected emailService: EmailService,
  ) {}

  public async findOne(id: string) {
    const order = await this.orderRepository.findOne({ where: { id } });

    if (!order) {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_FOUND');
    }

    return order;
  }

  public async create(args: { customerId: string; total: number }) {
    const customer = await this.customerProvider.findOne(args.customerId);

    const order = await this.orderRepository.create({
      values: { customerId: customer.id, total: args.total, status: 'PENDING' },
    });

    await this.emailService.send({ orderId: order.id, template: 'order_confirmation' });

    return order;
  }

  public async cancel(id: string) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);

    if (order.status === 'SHIPPED') {
      throw exception('ORDER_ALREADY_SHIPPED');
    }

    await this.paymentService.refund(order.id, order.total);

    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id },
      values: { status: 'CANCELLED' },
    });
  }

  public async refundPartial(id: string, amount: number) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);

    if (amount > order.total) {
      throw exception('REFUND_EXCEEDS_TOTAL');
    }

    await this.paymentService.refund(order.id, amount);

    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id },
      values: { refundedAmount: amount },
    });
  }
}

@start payment.service.ts
import { injectable } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';

@injectable()
export class PaymentService {
  public async refund(orderId: string) {
    const response = await this.http.post(`/refunds`, { orderId });

    if (response.status !== 200) {
      throw exception('REFUND_FAILED');
    }

    return response.data;
  }
}

@expected payment.service.ts
import { injectable } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';

@injectable()
export class PaymentService {
  public async refund(orderId: string, amount: number) {
    const response = await this.http.post(`/refunds`, { orderId, amount });

    if (response.status !== 200) {
      throw exception('REFUND_FAILED');
    }

    return response.data;
  }
}
